If the first character of the given string matches the first character of the first input string, it recursively checks the remaining characters of the given string and the first input string. Similarly, if the first character of the given string matches the first character of the second input string, it recursively checks the remaining characters of the given string and the second input string. If neither condition is met, it returns `False`. 

This solution has a time complexity of O(n * m) because it checks all possible combinations of characters from the two input strings. It handles cases where the input strings may contain duplicate characters and edge cases such as empty strings smoothly.

